    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **254 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `membershipNumber` is derived entirely from the owner's own already-stored fields (`customerCode` + `registrationDate`), so I surfaced it as a read-only response field computed in the mapper \u2014 the same pattern the codebase already uses for `displayName` and `initials`. No new entity column, DB migration, or pipeline step was needed, and it works identically for both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Two changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the getter/setter), documented as `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `membershipNumber` via an expression backed by a helper:\n   ```java\n   return String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", owner.getCustomerCode(),\n           owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);\n   ```\n   It returns `null` when either source field is absent, keeping seed/legacy owners safe. For a 2026 registration and code `SMI-0007`, this yields `SMI-0007-M26`, matching the spec and the new `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` assertion.",
